    "long_instructions": "# Choice: Design Your Own Path\r\n\r\nYour Task: A painter has a job to do in the neighborhood, and you decide the plan. Choose a path to paint, and write an `if`/`else` that helps the Painter do it. The bucket holds 8 units of paint, and each square you paint uses 1.\r\n\r\nYour program should:\r\n\r\n- Use an `if` with one of these checks: `can_move()`, `is_on_bucket()`, `has_paint()`, or `is_on_paint()`.\r\n- Use an `else` for when the answer is False.\r\n- Put a comment above your `if` that explains what the Painter is checking for.\r\n- Paint at least one square.\r\n\r\nDo This:\r\n\r\n1. Look at the map. Where do you want to paint a path? What will the Painter need to check along the way?\r\n2. Write your program. Decide what the Painter does when the answer is True and when it is False.\r\n3. Run your program. Check that the console shows no error. Which branch ran? Change something before your `if` so the other branch runs, then run it again.\r\n4. Use Validate to check your work.\r\n\r\nCoding Tip: The Painter can't move into the food truck or the planters, and it can't paint a square that still has a bucket with paint on it. Plan your path to avoid both.",
